I have everything needed. Here is the complete report on `customerCode` and owner identity.

## Summary / important note first

There is a **redesign in flight**. The current implementation builds `customerCode` as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, but the acceptance test (the target spec) requires `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. The test currently does not match the implementation.

- Target spec: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java:7,11,14` — `customerCode` must match `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` i.e. `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.
- Current impl produces `LON-SMI-0007`, which does NOT match that regex.

---

## 1. Where `customerCode` is defined and built

**Field definition** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:60-61` (`@Column(name = "customer_code") private String customerCode;`), getter/setter at lines 132-138.

**Construction** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` (full body):

```java
13  public class AssignCustomerCode {
15      public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
16          int sequence = countOwnersInCity(owner, ownerRepository) + 1;
17          String city3 = first3Upper(owner.getCity());
18          String last3 = first3Upper(owner.getLastName());
19          owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", city3, last3, sequence));
20      }
22      private static int countOwnersInCity(Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
23          String city = normalize(owner.getCity());
24          int count = 0;
25          for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
26              if (normalize(existing.getCity()).equals(city)) {
27                  count++;
28              }
29          }
30          return count;
31      }
33      private static String first3Upper(String value) {
34          String v = value == null ? "" : value;
35          return v.substring(0, Math.min(3, v.length())).toUpperCase();
36      }
38      private static String normalize(String value) {
39          return value == null ? "" : value.trim().toLowerCase();
40      }
41  }
```

**Current format/algorithm:** `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` — first 3 letters of city (upper), first 3 letters of last name (upper), and a 4-digit zero-padded per-city sequence = (count of existing owners in the same city) + 1. Example `LON-SMI-0007`.

**Where it runs in the create flow** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml:52-55` (step `assignCustomerCode`, runs after `applyRegistrationDate`, before `assignMembershipNumber`). The full ordered create pipeline is in that YAML file.

---

## 2. Things derived from customerCode

**Membership number** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java` (full body):

```java
12  public class AssignMembershipNumber {
14      public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
15          String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
16          owner.setMembershipNumber(owner.getCustomerCode() + "-M" + yy);
17      }
18  }
```
Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the registration year), e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`. Field defined `Owner.java:63-64`, getter/setter 140-146.

**Check digit** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java` (full body):

```java
11  public final class CustomerCodeCheckDigit {
13      private CustomerCodeCheckDigit() {
14      }
16      /** The check digit of an already-assigned owner's customer code. */
17      public static Integer of(Owner owner) {
18          String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
19          return customerCode == null ? null : luhn(customerCode);
20      }
22      /** Luhn check digit (0-9) over the decimal digits contained in {@code value}. */
23      static int luhn(String value) {
24          int sum = 0;
25          boolean dbl = true;
26          for (int i = value.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
27              char c = value.charAt(i);
28              if (c < '0' || c > '9') {
29                  continue;
30              }
31              int d = c - '0';
32              if (dbl) {
33                  d *= 2;
34                  if (d > 9) {
35                      d -= 9;
36                  }
37              }
38              sum += d;
39              dbl = !dbl;
40          }
41          return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
42      }
43  }
```
Luhn digit computed over only the decimal digits in `customerCode`. Exposed on the DTO via the mapper (see below). It is a derived/computed field, not stored on `Owner`.

**Create audit record** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` (full body):

```java
15  public class AuditOwnerCreated {
17      private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");
19      public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
20          AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
21                  owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
22                  owner.getMembershipLevel());
23      }
24  }
```
Emits on the dedicated `AUDIT` SLF4J logger after save (`owners.POST.yml:82-85`). Captured in tests by `AuditLogCapture` (see section 7).

**Locality derivation** — carried on the DTO via the mapper, not on `Owner`. `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java:27-34`:

```java
27  @Mapping(target = "locality",
28          expression = "java(LocalityLookup.regionOf(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode()))")
...
31  @Mapping(target = "identityKey",
32          expression = "java(OwnerIdentityKey.of(owner))")
33  @Mapping(target = "checkDigit",
34          expression = "java(CustomerCodeCheckDigit.of(owner))")
```
So `locality`, `identityKey`, and `checkDigit` are all computed at mapping time on `toOwnerDto`. Locality logic lives in `LocalityLookup` (section 4). Note locality is NOT derived from customerCode — it comes from city+postcode.

